The full reduction confirms a viable route, but not the triage’s proposed random-coordinate route. I’m using the paper’s own Section 1.4 logic-engine object and Section 4 equivalence: a compact armature-orientation program is a finite witness because the checker can expand its flag choices and test every row locally. I’m treating this honestly as a paper-licensed reduction (not native geometry coverage), and as Track B: the generated signed constraint graph has a linear-time propagation algorithm, while the intended shortcut is a hidden XOR-character invariant that keeps the by-hand route under 300 operations. I’m checking the repository’s exact gate/report expectations before implementing it.
