codex
The existing draft is not safe to ship: its block operator \(I+T_a+T_b\) is its own inverse over \(\mathbb F_2\), so the certificate is recovered directly by applying the displayed block twice in only \(2n\) XORs. That makes the reported 6.5-million-operation Gaussian baseline non-strongest and collapses the claimed Track B gap. I’m replacing that construction with an odd, dense translation convolution whose honest direct inverse costs about two million XORs at shipping size, while a quadratic-ANF invariant yields a short symbolic polynomial certificate.
