codex
Implemented a self-contained Track B generator based on the paper’s logic-engine reduction.

Key results:

- All local G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Shipping preset: `n=2048`, 11,479-operation reference algorithm versus a 215-operation structural route.
- G4: 0 hits in 200,000 samples; exact probability approximately `1.17e-167`.
- Five adversarial attacks failed across 8/8 seeds.
- Canonicalization passed 20/20 invariance, witness-carrying, and distinctness checks.
- The benchmark is honestly classified as a paper-licensed logic reduction, not native geometry coverage.
- The source is the substantive [arXiv v2 paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.15002v2); v3 is withdrawn.

Files:

- [gen_2510_15002.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2510.15002/gen_2510_15002.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2510.15002/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2510.15002/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2510.15002/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2510.15002/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2510.15002/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The only remaining blocker is external: every OpenRouter draw returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded,” so the three oracle arms have zero scored attempts. The result is locally verified but cannot honestly be called hardened or submission-ready until those runs are repeated with a replenished `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`.
