codex
The tightened generator now passes G1–G9(c), with a structure-aware answer space of \(2^{67}-1\) quadratic ANFs and 0 hits in 200,000 samples. I also corrected the no-tool effort accounting: the compact route is at most 268 scalar XORs, not 215, so `hard` is the last compliant rung; doubling still verifies, but rises to 321 operations and is correctly marked `cap_bound`. I’m moving to the script-owned oracle run now.
